Terraform mid level interview questions and answers.

1️⃣ Why do we use the Kubernetes provider in Terraform when we already have EKS in AWS or AKS in Azure?

Answer:
EKS and AKS are managed Kubernetes services, but they only provide the control plane. To manage Kubernetes resources (like deployments, services, and config maps) within the cluster, we use the Kubernetes provider in Terraform. It allows us to define and manage cluster resources declaratively, ensuring consistency and automation in infrastructure provisioning.

